<BaseLayout title="Search Data Benchmark #1 — Frozen Methodology" description="Frozen methodology for comparing DataForSEO, SE Ranking API and Mangools API on fixed search-data workloads.">
<section class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">SDB-B01 · Protocol frozen Sep 23, 2026</p><h1>Search Data Benchmark #1</h1><div class="notice"><strong>Status:</strong> methodology published; the comparable three-provider production workload has NOT been executed. No benchmark result or winner is claimed.</div>
<p>SDB-B01 is designed to compare DataForSEO, SE Ranking API and Mangools API without converting unlike proprietary metrics into a fake common score.</p>
<h2>Fixed environment</h2><p>United States, English and Desktop where the provider exposes those controls. Timestamps and sanitized raw evidence are retained. Missing, failed and limited calls remain in the evidence.</p>
<h2>Fixed keyword workload</h2><p>The protocol freezes 20 queries: serp api; best serp api; google serp api; seo api; best seo api; seo data api; keyword research api; rank tracking api; backlink api; search data api; ai search api; ai visibility api; ai search visibility; ai visibility tools; dataforseo api; se ranking api; mangools api; serp data api; search volume api; keyword data api.</p>
<h2>Six SERP deep dives</h2><p>serp api; best serp api; seo api; keyword research api; ai search api; dataforseo api. The target is the top 10 organic results when a provider supports a comparable API response.</p>
<h2>Measurements</h2><p>Response state, coverage, missing-field rate, top-10 URL/domain overlap, rank disagreement for shared URLs, search-volume disagreement, runner latency and observable request cost.</p>
<h2>Rules</h2><p>Provider-specific metrics retain their provider labels. There is no aggregate winner score. A protocol change requires a new version or a new benchmark; it cannot be silently made after results are seen.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>